==Trivia==
*Soybean Graveyard's Japanese name, Kinako Bochi (きなこ墓地, "Kinako Cemetery"), sounds similar to kinako mochi (きなこ餅), [[wikipedia:Mochi|mochi]] coated with ''[[wikipedia:Kinako|kinako]]'' (roasted soybean flour). It could also be a reference to [https://japanese-products.blog/2018/04/11/kinakobo-japanese-dagashi-candy/ kinakobō] (きなこ棒), a stick-shaped candy made using ''kinako''.

